{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8xOTk5LS1CZWZvcmUvUmVkJTJDJTIwV2hpdGUlMjBBbmQlMjBaZXJvJTIwJTI4MTk2NyUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"Red, White And Zero","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/aEGNZ1r7kdB43stYnE0SrOvrjqK.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6ShUsj3qKSxHsKPT9mfCw9RG3wX.jpg","description":"Composed of three shorts – Ride of the Valkyrie, The White Bus, and Red and Blue – from three of Britain’s most-celebrated directors - Lindsay Anderson, Peter Brook, and Tony Richardson.  Comic legend Zero Mostel stars as an opera singer (in full costume) navigating the London transport network as he attempts to reach Covent Garden in 'Ride of the Valkyrie'.  Scripted by Shelagh Delaney, 'The White Bus' blends realism, drama, and poetry as a despondent young woman travels home to the North of England.  And Vanessa Redgrave stars in Tony Richardson’s romantic reverie and musical featurette 'Red and Blue'. Produced in 1967, but ultimately shelved.\n\nRated 12 · Released 30 Jan 1968 · United Kingdom · Language: English · 98 min\nStudio: Holly Films, Woodfall Film Productions\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"1967","genres":["Comedy","Music","Drama","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"5.0","runtime":"98 min","cast":["Zero Mostel","Julia Foster","Frank Thornton","Patricia Healey","Arthur Lowe","John Sharp","Julie Perry","Stephen Moore"],"director":["Lindsay Anderson","Peter Brook"],"released":"1968-01-30T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Lindsay Anderson","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/l4R2RoLdqtY8xLrrt6v176tbtNQ.jpg"},{"name":"Zero Mostel","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/15kRWmicFWhV06o7kc1L8OOfulY.jpg"},{"name":"Julia Foster","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/kr45R39ia0pZ9nLfCIuUr444WaG.jpg"},{"name":"Frank Thornton","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/1B52SFlRkTQsgAw6MFbzsF1Kd2i.jpg"},{"name":"Patricia Healey","character":"The Girl","